the-firm-as-one-program-lines-16 : List (List Word)
the-firm-as-one-program-lines-16 = cons "  - **PE5** Proofs as optimizer information: assumptions become theorems." (cons "    - **PE5.1** Facts established during specialization: a length validated once, a field in range, buffers that do not alias, an aligned pointer, an impossible case." (cons "    - **PE5.2** Emitted as [[assume(...)]], __restrict, std::assume_aligned, std::unreachable(), constant trip counts, final, noexcept." (cons "    - **PE5.3** Today such hints are avoided or used in fear, because a wrong one is undefined behaviour the optimizer exploits. Here each is a proven precondition: the optimizer's appetite for undefined-behaviour assumptions becomes a source of speed instead of a hazard." (cons "    - **PE5.4** The C++ compiler receives the most information it can be given, and all of it is sound." nil))))
